{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01262",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 7.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.07,
      "end_seconds": 14.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.2,
      "end_seconds": 18.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a high temperature."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.44,
      "end_seconds": 27.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.86,
      "end_seconds": 41.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.48,
      "text": "for one week, I'd say i've also had a dry cough, for two days with dry cough, only honey, and it's not much"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.62,
      "end_seconds": 51.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Any diarrhoea, blue lips or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.71,
      "end_seconds": 55.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.0,
      "end_seconds": 58.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Have you had vomiting, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.39,
      "end_seconds": 61.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "No. No vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.29,
      "end_seconds": 66.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "and your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.02,
      "end_seconds": 70.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.68,
      "end_seconds": 74.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.35,
      "end_seconds": 85.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days. I swim twice a week. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.9,
      "end_seconds": 93.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.98,
      "end_seconds": 109.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for two years now. I have high blood pressure, for about ten years. Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.29,
      "end_seconds": 118.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.41,
      "end_seconds": 125.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "yes, cat fur, it gives me sneezing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.73,
      "end_seconds": 145.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.66,
      "end_seconds": 152.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "I had two stents put in my heart three years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.4,
      "end_seconds": 165.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Right, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.77,
      "end_seconds": 169.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Hydrochlorothiazide. I take it every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.37,
      "end_seconds": 172.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.09,
      "end_seconds": 185.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.81,
      "text": "It's 12.5 milligrams. It's aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day. It's Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 186.75,
      "end_seconds": 198.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "doctor, I've got the readings for you height 150 centimetres, saturation 93 percent, heart rate 95, weight 81 kilos, pressure 124 over 89, temperature 36.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.52,
      "end_seconds": 204.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.84,
      "end_seconds": 210.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.66,
      "end_seconds": 214.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.93,
      "end_seconds": 233.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.67,
      "text": "Your chest is clear apart from a few crackles at the right base and and your oxygen level is a bit low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.66,
      "end_seconds": 239.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.13,
      "end_seconds": 268.16,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.79,
      "end_seconds": 270.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.16,
      "end_seconds": 283.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 284.98,
      "end_seconds": 288.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I've already done a viral swab, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.85,
      "end_seconds": 300.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.29,
      "text": "Okay, great, that's useful. Rest, keep your fluids up and lie on your tummy or side to help your breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.39,
      "end_seconds": 314.51,
      "duration_seconds": 14.12,
      "text": "right, right. Come back or go to emergency straight away if you become more breathless or confused. Let's review you in two days. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.15,
      "end_seconds": 318.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "right, I'll do that thank you, doctor"
    }
  ]
}